.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operational databases.
#
# These are the *live* stores: they are rebuilt by fetching from the Blizzard
# API and they are measured in gigabytes.  Git is a source-code tool; a
# 4.4 GB binary blob in a commit is not reviewable, cannot be diffed, and
# makes every clone and every push pay for data that is derived anyway.
# The schema lives in code (`woweconomy/intel/store.py`), so a fresh checkout
# recreates an empty store and refills it with `scripts/intel.py`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
archives/
data/aggregates.sqlite
data/aggregates.sqlite-wal
data/aggregates.sqlite-shm

# Runtime state.  A lock file or a cursor position describes this machine at
# this second; committing it means the next pull fights the running pipeline.
data/watch.lock
data/watch_state.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build and test detritus.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/

# Logs: appended by whatever ran last, never a source of truth.
logs/
*.log

# Dated CSV backups written by the export scripts (`items.2026-10-21.bak.csv`).
csv/*.bak.csv
reports/**/*.bak.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch.  `attic/` holds the one-off probes and measurements that used
# to sit at the repo root; they are kept for reference but are not part of the
# system.  `data/_phase*` holds pre-migration backups and experiment output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/_*.py
/_*.txt
/_*.json
/file
storage_audit*.json
storage_audit*.txt
attic/
data/_phase*/
*.joblib

# Editor / OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
